-Originates from differential topology and Morse theory, applied to volume rendering to leverage the geometric properties of scalar fields. The classification of stationary points based on Hessian eigenvalues is a standard mathematical definition [S1, unofficial]. The concept of ascending and descending manifolds and the Morse-Smale complex further extends this to topological graph representation of scalar fields [S1, unofficial].
